  - ebpf
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NiShITa-code/cada_project"
abstract: >
  A head-to-head study of representation-level (text/LLM-judge) and effect-level
  (syscall) monitoring of LLM code-agents on real, executed attacks under an
  obfuscation ladder. Findings: the text-monitor obfuscation collapse is a
  capability/prompt-dependent decoding arms race; the syscall monitor's benign
  false-positive tax scales with agent autonomy (8% to 44%); a hybrid monitor that
  judges the decoded runtime arguments fixes both the arms race and the FP-tax
  (44% to 3%) and resists adaptive autonomous evasion, while inheriting
  effect-level monitoring's semantic blind spot.
